Z||000000||yo_sweet||12-11-2001||01:06 PM||||i posted about this before still haven't fixed the prob i turn the igntion back and i blow my no 10 red fuse , then the little round box on the rear firewall to the right starts smokeing , someone said soemthing about it being a cruise control siolond?? anyway i went to pontaic and didn't know if this was the item but they wanted $400 for it could someone help?<P>thanks<P>------------------<BR>1986 Fiero SE 2.8lv6<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/dance.gif">  <P><BR>www.geocities.com/acme_s2000/intro.html<BR>yo_sweet!||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroJoe||12-11-2001||01:20 PM||||You have a short to ground, coming from a +12v circuit that is on the radio circuit.  Look up the wiring diagram in a Helm or Haynes manual, and trace all those wires that are on that particular circuit.  Check for frayed, split or ruined wires that would be causing your problem.  Start at the cruise servo (if thats actually what you're talking about, I can't tell from you description), and trace those wires and check for the signs of shorting.||||reg||1
Z||000002||yo_sweet||12-11-2001||01:27 PM||||the little black box the cruise thing is cracked and burnt, thsi happend after i washed the motor||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroJoe||12-11-2001||01:35 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by yo_sweet:<BR><B>the little black box the cruise thing is cracked and burnt, thsi happend after i washed the motor</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The water from you washing your motor got into a connector and shorted out the circuit.  You have ruined your cruise servo then, not a hard part to find new though.  Take apart the connectors and dry them out.  Take caution next time you wash the engine compartment.||||reg||1
